 running every program with nocio present and matching the exact text`**** Can't install trap handler ****`.--------------------------------------------------------------KNOWN GOOD, WITH A CONDITION--------------------------------------------------------------  advent      reads advent1..4.txt from the CURRENT directory.              chd /dd/GAMES/ADV  first.  It was never broken.  hack        stats argv[0] after it changes directory, so invoke it by its              full path:  /dd/CMDS/GAMES/hack  aterm       WORKS.  Config ships in SYS/ATERM; run it from a login session.              `aterm /t1' for a real serial port  crib        both want TERM, so run them from a login session  cribbage  snake       WORKS in a login session; bus errors without TERMCAP  ksh         `ksh -c '<commands>'` works -- loops, variables, $PWD.  Its              INTERACTIVE loop prints no prompt and runs nothing here  cxref       wants a .c file; delbak finds *_bak files (OS-9 uses _bak)--------------------------------------------------------------NOT ON THIS DISK -- source exists but will not build--------------------------------------------------------------  hack     source damaged in all three surviving copies.  The BINARY works           and is in CMDS/GAMES.  phan     18 corrupt bytes across every source file; not reconstructable           without inventing source text.  cdecl    ANSI C source; Microware C is K&R.  m4       one copy aborts Microware cpp -- but the OTHER copy built, and           m4 IS on this disk.  Always check every copy.  zoo,fiz  the header defining struct item is absent.  gammon,  need BSD sgtty.h / a.out.h / sys/filsys.h -- interfaces OS-9  tet2,    never had, and which exist nowhere in this collection.  x10  elvis    full documentation and source are on the disk; no binary.  Full reasoning in SOURCES.txt.